			<key>label</key>
			<string>Main</string>
			<key>footerText</key>
		<string>SpringBoard-only build: one dylib is injected into SpringBoard only, so it cannot affect the boot chain or other apps. Three-Finger Swipe Down and the optional Volume Up + Down chord toggle recording. Built for rootHide Bootstrap (roothide) and Dopamine 2 (rootless) on iOS 15 to 17.</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>cell</key>
			<string>PSSwitchCell</string>
			<key>label</key>
			<string>Enable Tweak</string>
			<key>key</key>
			<string>enabled</string>
			<key>default</key>
			<true/>
			<key>defaults</key>
			<string>com.yourname.volumechordrecorder</string>
			<key>PostNotification</key>
			<string>com.yourname.volumechordrecorder.prefschanged</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>cell</key>
			<string>PSGroupCell</string>
			<key>label</key>
			<string>Privacy Indicator</string>
			<key>footerText</key>
			<string>Hides the iOS privacy indicator (the orange microphone dot and the green camera dot). Two mechanisms, chosen by what the running iOS actually has: the indicator views are forced to zero alpha where those classes exist, and where they do not (measured: none of them is present on iOS 16.4.1) SpringBoard's sensor-activity update is dropped instead, which is what makes it draw the dot in the first place. Off by default: with the switch off nothing is changed. Takes effect on the next indicator update; respring to clear a dot that is already on screen.</string>
		</dict>
