			<string>Audio Recording Quality</string>
			<key>footerText</key>
			<string>Codec and Bitrate decide how good a voice recording sounds. AAC with an explicit bitrate is the normal choice. ALAC and Linear PCM are lossless: no quality loss at all, but far bigger files, and Linear PCM also changes the container to .wav. Bitrate applies to AAC only. Stereo uses the iPhone microphone array; mono halves the size. Video audio is not affected: iOS has no movie-output audioSettings.</string>
